WEBVTT

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:06.034
EchoScribe started as my personal
vibe coding project.

00:00:06.396 --> 00:00:08.963
I wanted a tool for my own everyday
use,

00:00:09.092 --> 00:00:10.898
without another app subscription.

00:00:11.323 --> 00:00:13.117
Then I kept adding things I needed,

00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:14.097
and it grew.

00:00:14.458 --> 00:00:17.941
The job I return to most is simple:
take an

00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:19.837
article or a piece of text,

00:00:19.967 --> 00:00:20.933
get the main points,

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:22.830
and do something useful with them.

00:00:26.333 --> 00:00:27.649
Before the first summary,

00:00:27.752 --> 00:00:30.216
open Settings and choose your
provider.

00:00:30.577 --> 00:00:32.047
For this iPhone example,

00:00:32.215 --> 00:00:36.692
choose OpenAI and use its API key in
the OpenAI field.

00:00:37.117 --> 00:00:38.226
Keep the key hidden,

00:00:38.304 --> 00:00:39.594
then return to the app.

00:00:39.904 --> 00:00:41.955
There is no EchoScribe subscription;

00:00:42.149 --> 00:00:45.102
your provider bills API usage
separately.

00:00:45.876 --> 00:00:48.482
EchoScribe connects directly to that
provider,

00:00:48.521 --> 00:00:51.669
whose processing and retention
policies apply.

00:00:55.167 --> 00:00:57.244
Let's start with an article on
Android.

00:00:57.669 --> 00:00:58.340
In Chrome,

00:00:58.469 --> 00:00:59.488
open the menu,

00:00:59.656 --> 00:01:00.481
choose Share,

00:01:00.610 --> 00:01:02.261
and select EchoScribe.

00:01:02.688 --> 00:01:04.365
The link arrives in the app.

00:01:05.268 --> 00:01:08.260
EchoScribe retrieves the article text
and sends it to

00:01:08.325 --> 00:01:09.911
the provider for a summary.

00:01:10.583 --> 00:01:12.066
Now the result is ready.

00:01:15.634 --> 00:01:16.975
Read the main points here,

00:01:17.104 --> 00:01:19.813
or double-tap the summary to open the
reading view.

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:23.193
Scroll through the rest before moving
on.

00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:32.307
On iPhone,

00:01:32.332 --> 00:01:33.532
the task is the same,

00:01:33.661 --> 00:01:36.214
but the handoff uses Apple's share
menu.

00:01:37.660 --> 00:01:39.337
Open the article in Safari,

00:01:39.466 --> 00:01:40.291
choose Share,

00:01:40.343 --> 00:01:41.774
and tap EchoScribe.

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:47.419
The native Share Extension brings the
link into the app.

00:01:48.193 --> 00:01:51.301
Before sending content to a provider
for the first time,

00:01:51.533 --> 00:01:54.720
EchoScribe asks for your permission
on iPhone.

00:01:55.210 --> 00:01:55.997
Read the notice,

00:01:59.023 --> 00:02:01.461
then choose Allow and remember to
continue.

00:02:04.887 --> 00:02:08.034
The app processes the article and
displays the summary.

00:02:13.396 --> 00:02:16.001
Your choice is remembered for that
provider.

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:21.190
Let's keep working with this article.

00:02:21.616 --> 00:02:23.873
Choose a target language for the
result.

00:02:25.318 --> 00:02:27.666
EchoScribe translates the source text
and

00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:29.407
creates the summary in German.

00:02:32.769 --> 00:02:36.226
Play reads the current text aloud
through your voice provider.

00:02:40.651 --> 00:02:44.482
Open Share to see the available text
and audio options.

00:02:47.720 --> 00:02:49.642
History keeps your saved results.

00:02:52.068 --> 00:02:54.958
Reopen this article to continue where
you left off.

00:02:58.467 --> 00:03:00.273
You do not have to start with a link.

00:03:00.699 --> 00:03:01.873
Tap the microphone,

00:03:02.015 --> 00:03:02.711
speak,

00:03:03.767 --> 00:03:05.767
Please check the mobile layout by
Friday.

00:03:06.905 --> 00:03:08.763
and tap again to finish.

00:03:10.207 --> 00:03:10.685
Here,

00:03:10.814 --> 00:03:13.238
the spoken reminder becomes text.

00:03:16.013 --> 00:03:18.450
Switch to Summary to turn that
recording

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:20.283
into a short action item.

00:03:24.727 --> 00:03:26.210
Once the text is in the app,

00:03:26.249 --> 00:03:29.190
the same reading and sharing tools
are available.

00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:34.570
A spoken idea can become a picture,

00:03:34.597 --> 00:03:35.073
too.

00:03:35.848 --> 00:03:37.770
Here is a recorded description of a
friendly

00:03:37.834 --> 00:03:39.433
paper rocket above the Earth.

00:03:40.879 --> 00:03:44.593
Share the audio with EchoScribe and
let it transcribe the words.

00:03:47.826 --> 00:03:49.051
Check the transcript,

00:03:49.219 --> 00:03:50.406
then choose Image.

00:03:51.851 --> 00:03:53.592
The waiting time is sped up here.

00:04:00.019 --> 00:04:01.231
When the picture is ready,

00:04:01.399 --> 00:04:03.424
open it to take a closer look.

00:04:09.933 --> 00:04:12.564
You can shape the result with your
own prompts.

00:04:13.467 --> 00:04:15.647
Let's reuse the same spoken idea.

00:04:16.705 --> 00:04:17.983
Copy the transcript,

00:04:18.086 --> 00:04:20.446
then open Audio Prompt in Settings.

00:04:23.891 --> 00:04:27.567
Ask for three English bullet points:
subject,

00:04:27.735 --> 00:04:28.329
style,

00:04:28.354 --> 00:04:29.542
and constraints.

00:04:33.986 --> 00:04:35.031
Save the prompt.

00:04:37.805 --> 00:04:38.695
Back in the app,

00:04:38.785 --> 00:04:41.559
clear the view and paste the copied
text.

00:04:45.049 --> 00:04:48.867
EchoScribe processes it again using
your instructions.

00:04:51.229 --> 00:04:54.234
The new summary follows the format
you chose.

00:04:57.733 --> 00:04:58.649
On Android,

00:04:58.713 --> 00:05:02.016
two extra tools bring dictation into
other apps.

00:05:02.325 --> 00:05:04.583
With the EchoScribe keyboard enabled
and

00:05:04.661 --> 00:05:06.209
selected in a text field,

00:05:06.337 --> 00:05:07.924
dictate with its microphone.

00:05:13.285 --> 00:05:15.194
The result appears where you are
writing.

00:05:18.555 --> 00:05:20.582
Floating Dictation is another option.

00:05:20.891 --> 00:05:23.110
After granting its required
permissions,

00:05:23.252 --> 00:05:25.574
tap the floating microphone and
speak.

00:05:34.935 --> 00:05:36.561
Review the returned text,

00:05:36.637 --> 00:05:37.566
then insert it.

00:05:39.992 --> 00:05:42.804
The EchoScribe keyboard and Floating
Dictation

00:05:43.036 --> 00:05:45.113
are Android-only features.

00:05:48.633 --> 00:05:49.420
On iPhone,

00:05:49.587 --> 00:05:51.561
you can withdraw a provider's
permission in

00:05:51.652 --> 00:05:53.574
Settings to stop future sharing.

00:05:56.632 --> 00:05:58.515
That is the path I built EchoScribe

00:05:58.541 --> 00:06:00.799
around: bring in information,

00:06:00.927 --> 00:06:02.307
make it easier to use,

00:06:02.436 --> 00:06:04.372
and carry the result into your day.

00:06:04.797 --> 00:06:06.449
The project is open source,

00:06:06.539 --> 00:06:09.312
with code and setup instructions on
GitHub.
